That’s a solid proposal — optimizing quality based on device pixel ratio (DPR) can indeed reduce payload size without perceptible quality loss.

To build on your idea, you could make the logic slightly more dynamic and compatible with different image types or rendering contexts:

export default function customLoader({ src, width, quality = 80, dpr }) {
  // Adjust quality based on DPR
  let adjustedQuality;

  if (dpr >= 3) adjustedQuality = Math.round(quality * 0.5);
  else if (dpr >= 2) adjustedQuality = Math.round(quality * 0.65);
  else adjustedQuality = quality;

  return `https://example.com/${src}?width=${width}&quality=${adjustedQuality}`;
}


