The Suspense boundary is the contract: everything outside it is the static shell, everything inside it (plus any dynamic API it touches, like `cookies()`, `headers()`, or an uncached `fetch`) becomes the streamed dynamic hole. The most common gotcha is reading cookies or headers above the boundary, e.g. in the layout for an auth check. That silently bails the whole route out of PPR and you end up fully dynamic with no warning.

Keep the shell free of dynamic APIs and push each user-specific read into its own component behind its own Suspense, so they prerender the fallback and stream in independently. `unstable_noStore()` inside that component is the explicit way to mark a fetch as request-time if you're not using cookies/headers.

