`/api/og` reads `request.url`, so the result depends on the incoming request. That route cannot be meaningfully prerendered at build time unless every possible query-string variant is known ahead of time. With PPR enabled, Next tries to prerender what it can, hits the request-time read, and then bails out. Since the build still succeeds, the noisy part is the diagnostic message, not the runtime behavior.

For this route, I think the scoped fix is exactly:

```ts
// app/api/og/route.tsx
