export async function GET(request: Request) {
  const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url)
  // generate ImageResponse from searchParams
}
```

That is less blunt than it looks: placed inside `app/api/og/route.tsx`, it only marks that route handler as dynamic. It does not turn off PPR for the rest of the app.

If you have `cacheComponents: true` enabled and the warning still appears even with the route-level export, then I would reduce it to a minimal repro and file it as a logging/diagnostic bug. A route explicitly marked dynamic should not produce scary prerender bailout noise during `next build`.

So my recommendation would be: keep `force-dynamic` on request-dependent OG routes, and only look for another mechanism if you need static OG images with a known finite set of params.

