The issue: <body> must be a direct child of <html> in Next.js 14+. Wrapping it inside <Suspense> breaks the expected structure, causing the "Missing Root Layout Tags" error.

The fix (keeps static shell opt-out working):

```jsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        <Suspense fallback={null}>
          {children}
        </Suspense>
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

Why this still works: Moving <body> outside <Suspense> doesn't break the static shell opt-out. The shell (html + body) still renders statically. Only the children inside Suspense gets dynamic handling.

The docs example was correct for older versions. Your fix is correct for Next.js 14+. You can safely use the fix above.

```tsx
export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
 return (
 <html>
 <body>{children}</body>
 </html>
 )
}
```

