The syntax error is caused by passing an object `{provider.id}` to `toggleAccordion` when the function expects just the id value. Remove the extra braces and use the correct prop name (`eventKey` instead of `eventkey`). 

Here’s the corrected line (and a small tweak to keep the open state per item):

```tsx
<AccordionHeader
 as="h2"
 className="accordion-toggle"
 onClick={() => toggleAccordion(provider.id)}
 eventKey={provider.id}
 data-toggle="collapse"
 aria-controls="collapse-text"
 aria-expanded={selectedId === provider.id}
>
 {provider.name} {provider.description}
</AccordionHeader>
```

And adjust the toggle function to work with the id directly:

```tsx
function toggleAccordion(currentId: typeof provider.id) {
 setSelectedId(selectedId === currentId ? null : currentId);
}
```

Make sure `selectedId` is typed to match your id (e.g., `string | number | null`). This will resolve the parsing error and make the accordion toggle work as expected.

